{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root-cause investigation (2026-11-03, dev host, load average about 30-38, worktree at origin/main).\n\nThe idle time is not a sleep, polling interval, lock timeout, or subprocess grace period. It is git process startup cost on this host, multiplied by the number of git processes each test starts.\n\nObservations:\n- cProfile of test_server_never_pushes_and_workspace_is_isolated: 43.6 s of 54.4 s is select.poll inside subprocess.communicate, across 124 child processes. No time.sleep or lock wait appears.\n- GIT_TRACE2_EVENT over the same test: the 120 top-level git processes report about 4.5 s of git-internal runtime in total.\n- 25 runs of `/opt/homebrew/bin/git --version` from Python: 5.89 s wall vs 0.31 s git-internal. About 95% of each git call is spent before git's main or after it exits.\n- Exec median from Python: Homebrew git 0.11-0.33 s (max 1.3 s); /usr/bin/true 0.016 s; jq 0.016-0.018 s; plutil (also links CoreFoundation) 0.031 s. So the delay is specific to starting git on this host; CoreFoundation linkage alone does not explain it.\n- Spawns per test, measured: the test-side `_make_source` (git init + rebar.init_repo + create_ticket) starts about 52 processes (10-15 s); `jobs.run_job` starts 34-60 (7-14 s). Example: test_completion_pass_binds_server_derived_values = 112 spawns, 29.1 s.\n\nConsequence: a test-only change (build the authoritative source once per module, which the no-push assertions leave untouched) removes about 52 spawns per test, roughly 45% of the wall time. Estimated module total falls from about 310 s to about 170 s at this load. That does not meet the \"under 120 s\" AC; reaching it requires fewer git processes inside run_job (production: opcert_service workspace prepare + init ensures), or a faster git exec on the host."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793761752226354001,"uuid":"e819615c-e66d-4bbd-8fb8-15a8be6fff79"}